Z||000000||XDrewX||12-04-2001||01:58 PM||||I know someone has done this before, <BR>I would like to dye a set of seat belts red.<P>I have access to either the biege or the grey Fiero belts.<P>I am guessing I should use the Beige.<P>How is this done and what type of dye.<P>I want it to look OEM and not rub off or fade.<P>Thanks, <P>Andrew||||reg||1
Z||000001||Adrift||12-05-2001||12:45 PM||||If you use the search feature you'll find a discussion I started about a month ago...<BR>There are a few ways to do it, none of them that good.<BR>1) Spray them with Car Interior Dye (Tends to Peel off)<BR>2) Match a batch of very potent ritedye or some other dye and throw the belts in (Might be unsafe by changing the composition of the Nylon in the belt)<BR>3) Go to an apolstery shop, for $70 bucks they'll do the job for you AND take responsiblity of it screwing up||||reg||1
